IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fp-claims`
IMPORT `fp-qa`

-- Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (fp-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading a BOOLEAN, NUMBER or DATE input that is ASSUMEd stops the
-- evaluation with an error. Each question with a situation input is asked, for each role it is about, with the
-- situation FALSE and every later input ASSUMEd. Those two groups are generated from the parameter lists (scratchpad
-- qa_params.py) and come last. The hand-worked cases come first: each answer is worked by hand from the deposited
-- text, and for the claimant (the baseline's seat) each question is also asserted equal to the baseline export's answer
-- on the same facts. Life facts: d085 (Priya, Luca, Sofia), k084 (Jake, Ruby; the grant of 14 October 2052 is
-- HYPOTHETICAL), k098 (Tahlia), as in fp-cases-claims.l4; every other fixture is HYPOTHETICAL, including the $500 000
-- prescribed amount.
--
-- The baseline reads `Relationship`, `When I was born`, `Standing` and `Timing` through CONSIDERs with OTHERWISE, so an
-- ASSUMEd value of those would not fail if read (graffiti finding 31). They are read only after the role, which the
-- parameter script checks is read first.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked Relationship` IS A Relationship
ASSUME `an unasked When I was born` IS A `When I was born`
ASSUME `an unasked Standing` IS A Standing
ASSUME `an unasked Timing` IS A Timing

`as the claimant` MEANS `I am a family member who may have been left out of the estate, or left too little`
`as a beneficiary` MEANS `I take a share of the estate under the will or on intestacy`
`as the administrator` MEANS `I am the executor or administrator of the estate`

`the 14 October 2052 grant` MEANS Date 14 10 2052
`standing: yes` MEANS `yes: I am a person by whom an application may be made (s 7(1))`
`standing: no class` MEANS `no: I am not in any class that section 7(1) names`
`timing: in time` MEANS `in time: made within 6 months from the grant (s 7(2)(a))`
`timing: out of time` MEANS `out of time: it will not be heard unless the Court is satisfied the justice of the case requires leave, which I may seek at any time (s 7(2)(b), (3))`

`Luca, Daniel's son, as a record` MEANS `My position` WITH
    `my relationship to the deceased` IS `the deceased's child`
    `when I was born` IS `before the deceased died`
    `the deceased was maintaining me wholly or partly immediately before the death` IS FALSE
    `I was entitled to be maintained by the deceased at the death` IS FALSE
    `my parent, a child of the deceased, died before the deceased` IS FALSE
    `I was alive when the deceased married or began a de facto relationship with my parent` IS FALSE
    `the deceased took property from my parent's estate, not as a creditor` IS FALSE
    `the value of that property at my parent's death` IS 0
    `the parentage I rely on was admitted or established in the parent's lifetime` IS TRUE
    `the parentage I rely on arises under the Artificial Conception Act 1985` IS FALSE
    `as the parent, my parentage was admitted by the deceased as an adult or established in the deceased's lifetime` IS FALSE

§§ `For every role`

-- s 7(2)(a): the grant of 14 October 2052 (k084): 14 April 2053, for each role.
#ASSERT `What is the last day to claim without leave` `as the claimant` TRUE `the 14 October 2052 grant` EQUALS `by` (Date 14 4 2053)
#ASSERT `What is the last day to claim without leave` `as a beneficiary` TRUE `the 14 October 2052 grant` EQUALS `by` (Date 14 4 2053)
#ASSERT `What is the last day to claim without leave` `as the administrator` TRUE `the 14 October 2052 grant` EQUALS `by` (Date 14 4 2053)
#ASSERT `What is the last day to claim without leave` `as the claimant` TRUE `the 14 October 2052 grant` EQUALS `by` (`What is the last day I can apply without leave` `the 14 October 2052 grant`)

§§ `For the claimant`

-- s 7(1): Priya, the wife at the death (d085): yes. Luca, the son: yes. Sofia, the sister: no class. Jake, Graham's son
-- at 45 (k084): yes. Ruby, a granddaughter whose father is alive and whom Graham did not maintain: no class. Tahlia,
-- the former wife not maintained (k098): no class; a former wife receiving maintenance: yes.
